course: dictionary
lesson: 2492
title: One word, many meanings: deal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word deal has several meanings, so read the words around it to find the right one. «I'll do the dishes if you dry» is a deal: it is an agreement between two people, each doing a job for the other.
explain: In «When cards are dealt, each player gets the same number», deal means to hand out the cards to the players. The words cards and players are the clues.
explain: In «The Mole's thoughts ran a good deal on supper», a good deal means a lot. Check by swapping in a lot: «ran a lot on supper» still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Deal can be a noun (a deal, deals) or a verb (to deal, deals, dealt, dealing).
fact: A deal is an agreement between people, often when buying, selling or swapping. «It's a deal!» means you both agree.
fact: To deal cards means to give them out to the players in a game.
fact: «A great deal» or «a good deal» means a lot.
fact: To deal with something means to take action to sort it out. To deal with someone means to handle how they behave. «Big deal» and «no big deal» show whether something matters much.
exercise: «I'll do the dishes if you dry. It's a deal!» What is a deal here? | A card game | A plate of cold supper | A loud argument | *An agreement between two people
exercise: Mia deals the cards to four players. What does deal mean? | Keep the cards in a box | *Give them out to the players | Throw them away | Shuffle them into a tower
exercise: «The Mole's thoughts ran a good deal on supper.» What does a good deal mean? | Very little | *A lot | Nothing at all | A bargain
test: Sam had to deal with a broken bike before the race. What does deal with mean? | Sell it to a friend | Break it further | *Take action to sort the problem out | Ignore it
test: In «We made a deal», what kind of word is deal? | Verb | Adverb | *Noun | Adjective
exam: «It was no big deal when Toad splashed and rolled.» What does no big deal suggest? | It mattered very much | It was part of a card game | *It did not matter much | It was a bargain price
